            {
                "entry_id": "5f126b9f-6085-3074-b77e-5bca15d6df6f",
                "word": "thrutch",
                "pos": "verb",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "6f80e4c6-8be2-466b-be04-b83ca6869dae",
                        "entry_id": "5f126b9f-6085-3074-b77e-5bca15d6df6f",
                        "tags": [
                            "present",
                            "singular",
                            "third-person"
                        ],
                        "form": "thrutches"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "d324eef5-919c-4701-aead-56709289d6ad",
                        "entry_id": "5f126b9f-6085-3074-b77e-5bca15d6df6f",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "present"
                        ],
                        "form": "thrutching"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "1153f0ca-2620-4149-82cb-e1a74b8153b9",
                        "entry_id": "5f126b9f-6085-3074-b77e-5bca15d6df6f",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "thrutched"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "eb24ff63-3f83-4c6a-ad5c-a1debd1e4287",
                        "entry_id": "5f126b9f-6085-3074-b77e-5bca15d6df6f",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "thrutched"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cfe99f4f-8356-3edf-ab6e-64cf141af566",
                        "entry_id": "5f126b9f-6085-3074-b77e-5bca15d6df6f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To push; press; shove; thrust."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Northern-England",
                            "UK",
                            "dialectal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9e0a69dd-4de8-490c-bb09-d9442e4f3b61",
                                "sense_id": "cfe99f4f-8356-3edf-ab6e-64cf141af566",
                                "text": "If awd known wot aw know neaw, says Bobby, thrutchin his honds deep into his breeches pockets un hutchin up his shilders, theaw'd not ha getten me t' Knottmill fair."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "df8f1947-576b-4cac-8b48-e7c0abd2f549",
                                "sense_id": "cfe99f4f-8356-3edf-ab6e-64cf141af566",
                                "text": "GOOD. A class o' folk ut thinken theirsels so perfect they need no thrutch for t' get a front place i'th' top shop. But if they yerd th' trumpet seaund they'd be off like red-shanks; an' wouldno' care whoa they elbowed back at th' gates."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "45df9a17-6143-36f9-b570-a91f117e54bc",
                        "entry_id": "5f126b9f-6085-3074-b77e-5bca15d6df6f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To press or squeeze cheese in a vat."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Northern-England",
                            "UK",
                            "dialectal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "308390ab-6bf1-4589-9ad2-8e3d1340a4a0",
                                "sense_id": "45df9a17-6143-36f9-b570-a91f117e54bc",
                                "text": "Thrutchings.—To thrutch is to squeeze. The whey which is squeezed out of the cheese when under pressure and after being salted, is called thrutchings."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2654a1dc-4329-310a-9434-4087dea33c7f",
                        "entry_id": "5f126b9f-6085-3074-b77e-5bca15d6df6f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To crowd; throng; squeeze; huddle together."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Northern-England",
                            "UK",
                            "dialectal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f483875c-d753-418a-a14a-2d224e8a028d",
                                "sense_id": "2654a1dc-4329-310a-9434-4087dea33c7f",
                                "text": "Thir wur o lot o foke thrutchin reawnd summut; un aw thrutcht mi sel omung um , for to see whot wur gooin on."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "33aa32fc-10a1-4268-8bff-caf87a3c4f57",
                                "sense_id": "2654a1dc-4329-310a-9434-4087dea33c7f",
                                "text": "But, there it wur,—an' there it had to stop! for noather her nor me could stir a peg. ... Well; they olez say'n there's th' most thrutchin' wheer there's th' least reawm, an' it wur so theer, by th' mon;[…]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4a8ddd8b-3356-38d2-8e61-0b9816151873",
                        "entry_id": "5f126b9f-6085-3074-b77e-5bca15d6df6f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To trouble; oppress; distress."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Northern-England",
                            "UK",
                            "dialectal",
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e2578910-e1ac-483b-86dd-903ab402b96c",
                                "sense_id": "4a8ddd8b-3356-38d2-8e61-0b9816151873",
                                "text": "Then he grunted, an' mumble't, an' glendur't around,\nAn' he tooted about o'er th' neighbourin' ground;\nStill, never a soul to turn th' stone could he find,\nAn' it made him a little bit thrutched in his mind."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f9c46f69-9087-390d-bc60-498e4921962a",
                        "entry_id": "5f126b9f-6085-3074-b77e-5bca15d6df6f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To push, press, or squeeze into a place; move sideways or vertically in an upright position by wriggling the body against opposing rock surfaces. Compare chimney."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8e5b9f26-fd4d-464d-aa7f-4727aa3307c3",
                                "sense_id": "f9c46f69-9087-390d-bc60-498e4921962a",
                                "text": "I thrutched up the final crack to a small pinnacle."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
